{title: I’ll fly away}
{subtitle: Hymnal 311}
{x_theme: joy, praise}
{x_source: docx:1. Incomplete/I’ll fly away.docx}

{comment: Chorus}
I’ll fly away, O glory,
I’ll fly away
When I die, hallelujah, by and by
I’ll fly away

{comment: Verse 1}
Some glad morning when this life is over
I’ll fly away
To a home on God’s celestial shore
I’ll fly away

{comment: Verse 2}
When the shadows of this life is grown
I’ll fly away
Like a bird from prison bars has flown
I’ll fly away

{comment: Verse 3}
Just a few more weary days and then
I’ll fly away
To a land where joys shall never end
I’ll fly away
